or:#000\"> <br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        selectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;asset1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                    </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Select Asset1:&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                    choices </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mynames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                    selected</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;SPX&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>The problem I am having is that the above server.R code gets called when the app first fires up, at this point the user is presented with the first tab.  But when the user selects the second tab containing the uiOutput the selecinput dropdown seems to be removed, resulting in there being no selected input values.  The dropdown does get re-rendered to the screen but after the plot requiring the input has tried to render, creating an error because the input from the selectinput is NULL at the time.  The